# `The forty inventive principles and the four separation principles of TRIZ,`
# `as link data (issue #1138 B12, plan 12 leaf 16; #901).`
#
# `#901 asks for contradictions to be links carrying a value on a 0-1 range,`
# `and for the resolution shapes to be data rather than Rust branches. These`
# `are those shapes. src/selection_heuristics.rs names no principle — it reads`
# `an identifier out of this file, which is what makes the catalogue`
# `forgettable and rediscoverable -- delete it, rediscover it through the`
# `sources registry's wikipedia source from the article each row names, replay`
# `offline, and the content hash matches.`
#
# `resolves names the criterion pair a principle is classically applied to,`
# `where one is known; a row with no established pair carries none rather`
# `than inventing one. The criterion slugs are the ones`
# `data/seed/meanings-selection-criteria.lino grounds.`
